{"agent_id":"pp3g-LES2-doc-task-for-issue-314-write-a-self-contained-a685","agent_seq":5,"timestamp":"2026-08-09T15:55:40.469509679Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"497dbef5-069b-4086-b9f5-f2c54953d182","comment_uuid":"2861954e-33bd-452b-ae4e-1c3843dd3084","author":"pp3g-LES2-doc-task-for-issue-314-write-a-self-contained-a685","content":"Result: deliverable committed at 4cbae85 — docs/research/agent-tooling-and-permission-enforcement.md (697 lines, self-contained for external review).\n\nPOINTER: docs/research/agent-tooling-and-permission-enforcement.md\n\nContents:\n1. PURPOSE — four-role permission model (orchestrator plans/coordinates, builder implements, reviewer+auditor read-only verification), workflow-topology pre-positioned auditor (position store, staleness trigger, one-role/two-phase, readiness audit), git write discipline (commit gated on active issue; push/rebase/reset/clean/checkout/restore/stash/tag/am/apply/branch-delete blocked), model discipline (verified IDs, no free-tier for agent work).\n2. SOFTWARE STACK — opencode pp3g fork 1.18.13-pp3g-fork (verified via --version) + separate fork DB (opencode-fork-pp3g.db vs main opencode.db, #313), crosslink fork CLI v0.9.0-beta.1-59-g6221309e, the ~86-line claude bash wrapper (strict model enforcement, memory scope, CROSSLINK_AGENT_TYPE export, drops --allowedTools), rtk 0.40.0, sqlite3 stores, the three in-repo guard plugins, user-level model-whitelist plugin (~/.config/opencode/plugins/plugin.ts).\n3. ENFORCEMENT LAYERS — (a) opencode native engine reading agent .md frontmatter; (b) orchestrator-guard write blocking (#33677 gap); (c) crosslink-guard git/bash/issue enforcement (10-step priority, per-session agent tracking, by_type overrides); (d) rtk-guard fail-open rewrite; (e) hook-config.json as config source; (f) KICKOFF path: build_allowed_tools() -> --allowedTools string, separate surface from the .md blocks.\n4. WHY THIS SET — per-component table with the failure each prevents and evidence (#33677, #156 silent-hang epic, git discipline, active-issue gating, rtk token cost, model whitelist, #298 sleep grant).\n5. IDENTIFIED PROBLEM AREAS — THREE-SURFACE kickoff enforcement (hook-config allowed_bash_prefixes vs kickoff.allowed_tools vs .md block; observed: --allowedTools constructed by fork but dropped by wrapper, kickoff.allowed_tools currently UNSET in ASES); PER-TYPE ASYMMETRY (build_allowed_tools has no agent_type param — auditor-only grants not expressible without fork change); TWO-SURFACE INCONSISTENCY (.md claims 'opencode *'/'git *' but kickoff grants no opencode */sqlite3/stat/ps; concrete #313 evidence: Phase-1 auditor pp3g-dZ3X 'sqlite3 blocked by bash permission pattern (no allow rule for sqlite3)', fell back to stat-level verification); #33677 GAP requiring the custom plugin; CROSS-REPO DRIFT RISK.\n6. WHAT-NOT-TESTED / OPEN QUESTIONS — per-type allowedTools unimplemented; guard testability unaudited; rtk-guard x crosslink-guard hook ordering unmeasured; --allowedTools enforcement semantics; relaxed-mode allowlist nuance; free-tier 401 characterization; fail-open kill/pause paths.\n7. Verified-sources appendix (12 items).\n\nKey verified facts beyond the brief: kickoff.allowed_tools is NOT set in ASES hook-config.json (no 'kickoff' key); the deployed claude wrapper currently discards --allowedTools and opencode run exposes no such flag (so the fork-constructed surface is dormant in this deployment); agent tracking_mode is relaxed (allowlist not the blocking layer for agents; native .md deny is). READ-ONLY investigation — only the deliverable doc was written. Commit ref: 4cbae85.","created_at":"2026-08-09T15:55:40.462387531Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:lluBr/C5VCnLCknLgnyVDX0i2uqY9gGAgClmiE8zBtw","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgYpeVnRCHdDi2+itj7ZAvfLkrUgwl4aIm70UTw7cqftoAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAE7LkOnhzHnnGOedNnzYm3GvsuzXXT/vbMm9qmiJdHI1AcJXjnI3j18IEH9